WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,375
Intelligence must be packaged for the audience and the decision.

2
00:00:04,375 --> 00:00:10,023
A long technical report may be useful to an analyst but ineffective for an executive.

3
00:00:10,023 --> 00:00:15,830
A short executive summary may clarify risk but be too vague for detection engineering.

4
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:31,343
Useful CTI products include short reports, briefings, tickets, detection stories, watchlists, blocklists, executive summaries, incident response notes, vulnerability prioritization memos, and threat hunting hypotheses.

5
00:00:31,343 --> 00:00:33,888
The format should match the workflow.

6
00:00:33,888 --> 00:00:38,502
Operational teams often need intelligence in task-shaped formats.

7
00:00:38,502 --> 00:00:48,685
A detection engineer may need a behavior description, expected telemetry, example fields, ATT&CK mapping, false-positive notes, and test guidance.

8
00:00:48,685 --> 00:00:55,446
A SOC analyst may need triage steps, enrichment context, affected assets, and escalation criteria.

9
00:00:55,446 --> 00:01:05,708
A vulnerability manager may need evidence of exploitation, affected products, exposure context, compensating controls, and a recommended priority.

10
00:01:05,708 --> 00:01:10,084
Packaging is part of the intelligence work, not an afterthought.

11
00:01:10,084 --> 00:01:12,947
Good packaging also makes limits visible.

12
00:01:12,947 --> 00:01:23,448
If a watchlist includes indicators, it should explain how old they are, what source they came from, whether they are recommended for blocking or enrichment,

13
00:01:23,448 --> 00:01:26,153
and what false positives are plausible.

14
00:01:26,153 --> 00:01:34,903
If an executive summary describes a threat trend, it should explain confidence, business relevance, and what decision is needed.

15
00:01:34,903 --> 00:01:40,313
A product that hides uncertainty can look polished while making action riskier.

16
00:01:40,313 --> 00:01:44,210
STIX and TAXII are common concepts in structured sharing.

17
00:01:44,210 --> 00:01:53,041
STIX, the Structured Threat Information Expression, provides a way to represent threat intelligence objects and relationships.

18
00:01:53,041 --> 00:02:00,996
TAXII, Trusted Automated Exchange of Intelligence Information, supports exchanging that structured information.

19
00:02:00,996 --> 00:02:08,075
These standards can help organizations share and automate parts of CTI, but they do not replace analysis.

20
00:02:08,075 --> 00:02:13,167
A well-formatted object can still be stale, irrelevant, or low confidence.

21
00:02:13,167 --> 00:02:14,758
Handling rules matter.

22
00:02:14,758 --> 00:02:21,758
The Traffic Light Protocol, or TLP, is used to communicate how shared information may be redistributed.

23
00:02:21,758 --> 00:02:32,895
At a practical level, TLP:CLEAR can be shared broadly, TLP:GREEN is limited to the community, TLP:AMBER is limited to those who need it to protect their organization,

24
00:02:32,895 --> 00:02:37,589
and TLP:RED is restricted to named recipients or a very limited group.

25
00:02:37,589 --> 00:02:42,521
Teams must follow the version and policy used by their sharing community.

26
00:02:42,521 --> 00:02:48,248
Speed should not override accuracy, sensitivity, privacy, or source restrictions.

27
00:02:48,248 --> 00:02:52,942
During an incident, it can be tempting to forward everything quickly.

28
00:02:52,942 --> 00:02:59,465
That can expose sensitive investigations, violate sharing terms, or spread unverified claims.

29
00:02:59,465 --> 00:03:02,408
Good CTI sharing is timely and disciplined.

30
00:03:02,408 --> 00:03:11,954
It states confidence, marks handling requirements, protects sensitive details, and gives the recipient enough context to act responsibly.

31
00:03:11,954 --> 00:03:16,568
The best format is usually the format that fits an existing workflow.

32
00:03:16,568 --> 00:03:20,227
If engineers work from tickets, create a clear ticket.

33
00:03:20,227 --> 00:03:24,443
If executives make decisions from short briefs, write a brief.

34
00:03:24,443 --> 00:03:30,092
If detections are managed as stories with acceptance criteria, use that structure.

35
00:03:30,092 --> 00:03:34,546
CTI gains power when it moves through channels people already use.
